From 591958d5a220b1772f432537ba39dab2f60ec6c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=D0=B7=D0=B3?= <sreddev@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:57:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Harmony 600: read-only import of its arch-14 GSPM
 configuration

The 600 stores the Harmony One's GSPM image at another base (0x030000),
header constant (0x1400) and an 18-slot master index, with no touch
section. The harmony_600 backend runs the One's reader under that
layout: its slot map, three-atom command objects, presses with no
lead-in, six-byte section-6 slots, the 600's 54 scan codes (from
harmony-explorations, MIT), an LCD glyph-shape table, side-key labels
naming commands and activity names from their start screens.

The profile is read-only and build_project refuses, so nothing is built
or written for the 600. Format reference: docs/harmony_600/README.md.

Known gap: the backend imports harmony_one, so removing that backend
breaks this one (tests/test_removability.py); not ready for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
